---
import TextPage from '~/layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { CONTACT, TEL_HREF } from '~/config/site';

const path = '/delivery-information/';
---

<TextPage
  title="Delivery Information | Cone Sleeves UK"
  description="How Cone Sleeves UK delivers printed packaging across the UK, how dates are given, and what affects transit to your postcode."
  path={path}
  h1="Delivery Information"
  standfirst="How orders reach you, how dates are given, and why we do not publish a delivery promise."
  updated="2026-08-13"
  crumbLabel="Delivery Information"
>
  <h2>How orders travel</h2>
  <p>
    Finished goods are dispatched on national carriers to any address in the United
    Kingdom. We do not operate our own delivery vehicles and we have no regional depots, so
    every order is carried by a third party from production to your door.
  </p>
  <p>
    Packaging ships flat wherever the format allows it. That keeps the carriage cost down,
    protects the printed face, and means a pallet's worth of sleeves arrives in far less
    space than the same quantity pre-formed.
  </p>

  <h2>Why there is no published delivery time</h2>
  <p>
    Two separate periods sit between an order and a delivery, and only one of them is about
    transport.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Production</strong> — set by the print method, the run length, whether tooling
      is needed and how busy the press is that month. This is the larger of the two and it
      varies considerably.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transit</strong> — the carrier's own service, which is broadly consistent for
      mainland addresses and longer for some postcodes.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because production dominates, a single site-wide figure would be misleading. Your
    production lead time is confirmed in writing on your quotation, against your actual
    specification, and the carrier's transit is added to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Dates are estimates, not guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    Any delivery date we give is the carrier's estimate. We do not offer timed, next-day or
    same-day delivery anywhere in the UK, and we would rather say so plainly than imply a
    service we cannot control.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a date genuinely matters — an event, a seasonal launch, a shop opening — tell us at
    enquiry stage rather than at order stage. We schedule production backwards from a fixed
    date, and the artwork deadline that follows from it is usually earlier than people
    expect.
  </p>

  <h2>Postcodes that take longer</h2>
  <p>
    Transit to English, Welsh and lowland Scottish mainland addresses is broadly the same.
    These take longer, and some carriers apply a surcharge:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Scottish Highlands and Islands.</li>
    <li>Northern Ireland.</li>
    <li>Isle of Man, Isle of Wight, Channel Islands and the Scilly Isles.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We confirm what applies to your specific postcode when we quote, rather than leaving it
    to appear later as an unexpected cost.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery access</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us at order stage if your address has anything a carrier needs to know about:
    restricted access, a booking-in requirement, a delivery window, no forklift, or a
    city-centre location with vehicle restrictions. We can pass instructions on, though we
    cannot commit the carrier to a specific time.
  </p>

  <h2>Checking your delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Please check goods on arrival rather than after storing them. Shortages and transit
    damage need reporting promptly so that a claim with the carrier is still possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    If what arrives does not match the approved proof or the agreed specification, see our
    <a href="/returns-and-refunds/">returns and refunds page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Split deliveries</h2>
  <p>
    Splitting an order across two or more deliveries is often possible, and it suits
    seasonal businesses that would otherwise pay to store stock through a quiet period. It
    costs a little more per unit than a single delivery. Ask us to price both ways.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions about a delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Call <a href={TEL_HREF}>{CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</a> or email
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> with your order reference and we
    will chase the carrier on your behalf.
  </p>
</TextPage>
